  "metadata": {
    "job": "Tumbler wrap, ⌀80",
    "revision": "A",
    "notes": "The canvas height IS the circumference (π × 80), so a line spanning it closes on itself when the sheet rolls up — that is why the rings are lines, not circles. Twelve ticks, not thirteen: a tick at the top edge is the same line on the rod as the one at the bottom. Change the diameter and the canvas height must follow."
  },
